1
00:00:21,367 --> 00:00:23,767
[MARLA]<i> In order for
</i> a compound to be pure,

2
00:00:23,767 --> 00:00:27,733
<i>it has to undergo a tedious
process of removing impurities.</i>

3
00:00:28,367 --> 00:00:30,533
<i>In organic chemistry,
we call this,</i>

4
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,633
<i> purifying organic compounds.</i>

5
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,767
<i> In life, we call it, purging?</i>

6
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,133
<i>And maybe what I am
experiencing right now</i>

7
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:42,500
<i> is the painful act of purging.</i>

8
00:00:43,067 --> 00:00:45,667
<i> To rise, I have to fall first.</i>

9
00:00:46,067 --> 00:00:47,767
<i> To be truly alive,</i>

10
00:00:47,767 --> 00:00:49,733
<i> I have to die first.</i>

11
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:52,067
<i> Die?</i>

12
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:53,067
<i> Death?</i>

13
00:00:53,067 --> 00:00:54,667
<i> Is this the end for me?</i>

14
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,767
<i> No.</i>

15
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:58,567
<i> This can't be.</i>

16
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,200
<i>Would this moron's face
be the last thing I'd see</i>

17
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,567
<i> on my last day on earth?</i>

18
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:04,167
<i> No!</i>

19
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:07,167
<i>This is just part
of the purifying process.</i>

20
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,267
<i>Which process am I in right now?</i>

21
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:12,533
<i> Distillation?</i>

22
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:14,467
<i> Crystallization?</i>

23
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:16,033
<i> Chromatography?</i>

24
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:17,533
<i> Sublimation?</i>

25
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:18,667
<i> Extraction?</i>

26
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:20,800
<i> Or...</i>

27
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,333
<i> just plain realization?</i>

28
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:27,767
<i>Realization that
this Cole is not the same Cole</i>

29
00:01:27,767 --> 00:01:29,733
<i>that I fell in love
with years ago.</i>

30
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:33,333
<i>Maybe I was too
in love to see it.</i>

31
00:01:35,767 --> 00:01:37,767
<i> Explain that, science!</i>

32
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:38,767
[COLE GRUNTS]

33
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:39,767
[CRASHES]

34
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:46,733
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

35
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:56,833
[GASPS]

36
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:01,267
What are you doing here?

37
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:05,533
Marla, I'm here to apologize.

38
00:02:05,533 --> 00:02:06,700
[MARLA] Apologize?

39
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,300
Because you hurt me?

40
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,200
[COLE] No!

41
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,267
I could never do that
to you, Marla.

42
00:02:11,467 --> 00:02:12,367
So what?

43
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:13,767
I did this to myself?

44
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,400
[COLE] Marla,
I did everything to save you,

45
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,367
but I didn't get there in time.

46
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,167
Remember?

47
00:02:20,167 --> 00:02:23,167
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:24,133
Marla...

49
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,600
I'm sorry for everything I said.

50
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,867
My emotions just got
the better of me.

51
00:02:28,867 --> 00:02:30,833
That's why I said
those things, Marla.

52
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:33,300
I thought you were
behind that stunt

53
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:35,433
just to get back at me, right?

54
00:02:36,867 --> 00:02:38,200
Marla.

55
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,467
Marla, you're not
the only victim here.

56
00:02:41,467 --> 00:02:43,833
You're not the only one
who got hurt, Marla.

57
00:02:44,633 --> 00:02:46,600
I was hurt as well.

58
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,800
You know that physical injury
can heal faster

59
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:53,367
compared to
my emotional feelings, Marla.

60
00:02:54,267 --> 00:02:55,600
I'm a victim, too.

61
00:02:58,567 --> 00:02:59,700
In fact...

62
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,800
I'm more of a victim than you.

63
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:07,400
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,767
What are you doing here?

65
00:03:09,467 --> 00:03:10,800
- Marla, are you okay?
- Hey!

66
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:12,133
[NYX] Get out!

67
00:03:13,867 --> 00:03:15,833
Marla, I'm going
to ask you again.

68
00:03:16,233 --> 00:03:18,600
Are you involved with
what happened to Lester?

69
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,500
I said no!

70
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:24,800
But we're good.

71
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:27,600
Right?

72
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,900
Cole, you know, with everything
that's happening...

73
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,500
I need space.

74
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,800
I need to think.

75
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:41,767
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

76
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,767
Marla.

77
00:03:43,967 --> 00:03:44,967
Space?

78
00:03:44,967 --> 00:03:45,933
To think?

79
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:47,333
[APRIL] What for?

80
00:03:47,333 --> 00:03:49,467
Even after what he did to you?

81
00:03:49,467 --> 00:03:50,433
[NYX WHISTLES]

82
00:03:50,633 --> 00:03:51,733
Shh.

83
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:52,833
Relax.

84
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:56,267
Let's not pressure Marla
just yet.

85
00:04:08,833 --> 00:04:10,367
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

86
00:04:10,567 --> 00:04:11,733
Girls.

87
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:13,300
Be honest.

88
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,800
Did you do that to Lester?

89
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:22,800
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

90
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,933
[MARLA CLEARS THROAT]

91
00:04:24,567 --> 00:04:26,400
[SCOFFS] Okay, fine.

92
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,967
Yes. It was us.

93
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,333
I knew it!

94
00:04:29,533 --> 00:04:31,833
- I knew it.
- Nothing happened anyway.

95
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:34,600
Cole and Lester aren't
facing any consequences.

96
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,000
It's being covered up.

97
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,333
They reduced it as a prank.

98
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:38,467
Exactly.

99
00:04:38,467 --> 00:04:41,433
They say Principal Mckenna's
hunting down everyone

100
00:04:41,433 --> 00:04:43,567
who's involved with the torture

101
00:04:43,567 --> 00:04:44,467
of her baby boy.

102
00:04:44,467 --> 00:04:47,267
But we were all there
at the party.

103
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:49,867
I mean, stargazing.

104
00:04:50,267 --> 00:04:53,667
So, I think,
we're covered by our alibis.

105
00:04:53,667 --> 00:04:54,767
Alibi?

106
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,400
Daphne, you too?

107
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,800
I just learned that night,

108
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,800
when April talked to me.

109
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,767
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

110
00:05:02,833 --> 00:05:03,967
<i> Hi, Daphne.</i>

111
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:05,733
[DAPHNE] Hi?

112
00:05:07,667 --> 00:05:10,067
[APRIL]<i> Oh, I have
</i> to show you something.

113
00:05:10,067 --> 00:05:11,433
<i> Can we talk?</i>

114
00:05:11,433 --> 00:05:16,833
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

115
00:05:16,833 --> 00:05:17,967
Girl?

116
00:05:19,667 --> 00:05:21,667
[NYX] I'm sorry,
I forgot to return this.

117
00:05:21,667 --> 00:05:23,667
It was a back-up plan in case...

118
00:05:23,667 --> 00:05:25,067
you didn't Agree-ana Grande.

119
00:05:25,067 --> 00:05:26,900
- You scared me, girl.
- Sorry.

120
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:29,500
I kept looking for this.

121
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,833
You know how
I can't afford a new one.

122
00:05:31,833 --> 00:05:33,400
- I'm sorry.
- [DAPHNE CLICKS TONGUE]

123
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,800
It's okay.

124
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:37,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

125
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:39,400
To be honest...

126
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,800
I feel afraid every time...

127
00:05:42,833 --> 00:05:45,400
every time I see Lester.

128
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,800
So he deserved it.

129
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,033
[DAPHNE] Somehow, at least...

130
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,867
we got him to admit things?

131
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,033
Isobel...

132
00:05:57,433 --> 00:05:58,833
are you okay?

133
00:05:58,833 --> 00:06:05,433
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

134
00:06:05,433 --> 00:06:07,400
Are you okay, Marla?

135
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,433
Yeah.

136
00:06:11,467 --> 00:06:13,600
The doctor told me
there's no major injury,

137
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,967
so I'll be fine in
maybe a week or two.

138
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:21,567
I'm sorry.

139
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,033
[NYX] Girl!

140
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:26,000
- You apologized! Oh, my God!
- Okay, okay.

141
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,800
- Calm down, girl.
- First time.

142
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:31,400
It wasn't part of the plan
to get you hurt.

143
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:35,800
It was...

144
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,467
careless of me.

145
00:06:38,433 --> 00:06:39,567
I'm sorry.

146
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:44,500
Why are you even apologizing?

147
00:06:45,167 --> 00:06:47,533
You weren't the one who hurt me.

148
00:06:47,533 --> 00:06:48,500
Cole did.

149
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:50,700
I still feel...

150
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:51,833
guilty.

151
00:06:52,867 --> 00:06:53,867
[ISOBEL EXHALES SHARPLY]

152
00:06:53,867 --> 00:06:55,433
[MARLA] Well, you shouldn't be.

153
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,733
Anyway, speaking of Cole.

154
00:06:58,933 --> 00:07:00,733
He's denying everything.

155
00:07:00,933 --> 00:07:03,733
[MARLA] So, I'm hoping
we have surveillance video?

156
00:07:03,933 --> 00:07:05,033
Oh.

157
00:07:05,767 --> 00:07:07,433
[APRIL] I kind of...

158
00:07:07,433 --> 00:07:09,433
disabled all
the security cameras...

159
00:07:09,433 --> 00:07:11,067
so we won't get caught.

160
00:07:11,067 --> 00:07:12,900
So, we won't get any evidence.

161
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,000
I'm so sorry.

162
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,067
[DAPHNE] Damn it.

163
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,900
Why is it that...

164
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:20,533
we're always on the losing side?

165
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:23,067
The system is against us.

166
00:07:23,633 --> 00:07:25,767
[INHALES DEEPLY] Well, girls,

167
00:07:25,767 --> 00:07:28,033
better get ready for a long

168
00:07:28,033 --> 00:07:29,700
and bloody fight.

169
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:30,933
[NYX] Hey! Wait!

170
00:07:30,933 --> 00:07:32,167
Wait a minute.

171
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:33,700
Hold on that thought,

172
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:35,500
in the name of Beyoncé.

173
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,833
[NYX] Can you...

174
00:07:37,833 --> 00:07:41,100
hold your bloody thought
and bloody privates as well?

175
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:43,433
Because, you know,

176
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:45,800
this might be
our special reunion!

177
00:07:46,667 --> 00:07:48,667
Comeback, you know,
of the girl group?

178
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:49,833
This is it.

179
00:07:50,567 --> 00:07:52,867
This is our comeback,
I can feel it!

180
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:53,867
[NYX SQUEALS]

181
00:07:53,867 --> 00:08:00,833
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

182
00:08:10,467 --> 00:08:17,433
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:08:55,300 --> 00:09:02,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:09:02,267 --> 00:09:04,233
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

185
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:09,667
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

186
00:09:09,867 --> 00:09:16,067
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

187
00:09:16,067 --> 00:09:17,067
[SNIFFLES]

188
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,833
[COLE] April.

189
00:09:20,133 --> 00:09:22,867
How do you like your new room?

190
00:09:25,867 --> 00:09:27,167
It's great, yeah?

191
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:31,100
I think you very much
deserve it like this, April.

192
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,767
You monster!

193
00:09:36,767 --> 00:09:38,700
What's wrong with you, Cole?!

194
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:40,867
- [EXHALES SHARPLY]
- [COLE SINISTER LAUGHTER]

195
00:09:40,867 --> 00:09:43,133
What's wrong with me?!

196
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:45,133
I knew it.

197
00:09:47,633 --> 00:09:51,333
You were the ones behind
what happened to Lester,

198
00:09:51,333 --> 00:09:52,600
right?

199
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:56,900
And I know only Isobel
could come up

200
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,933
of that naughty
and cruel method.

201
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,133
And I know only Nyx
has the skill...

202
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,867
to build a machine like that.

203
00:10:08,067 --> 00:10:09,233
April...

204
00:10:10,967 --> 00:10:13,333
I am so close
to achieving my goals.

205
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,200
And nobody,

206
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,767
will ever get in my way.

207
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:22,867
[BOTH LAUGHING WRYLY]

208
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:24,767
Don't be so sure, Cole.

209
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:27,300
Because we will do everything...

210
00:10:28,167 --> 00:10:29,600
...to bring you down.

211
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:33,867
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

212
00:10:33,867 --> 00:10:35,300
Oh no, I'm scared.

213
00:10:35,333 --> 00:10:36,833
I'm so afraid of you, April!

214
00:10:36,833 --> 00:10:38,100
I'm so scared!

215
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:45,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

216
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,967
You see this?

217
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,933
Sir beat me up once again...

218
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:54,933
and threatened...

219
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:57,167
...to put me in the military.

220
00:10:57,933 --> 00:10:59,267
No.

221
00:10:59,267 --> 00:11:00,700
Of course...

222
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,067
I won't let that happen!

223
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:03,733
Why?

224
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,767
You deserve it!

225
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,300
You deserve it more.

226
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:10,833
I didn't deserve that.

227
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,067
Dad doesn't give a shit
about me.

228
00:11:14,833 --> 00:11:15,833
Okay.

229
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,100
Consider this as a warning.

230
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:23,400
If I go down,

231
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:27,900
I'll make sure all of you
will go down with me.

232
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:31,400
And tell this to your
crazy friends,

233
00:11:32,167 --> 00:11:33,833
that this is war.

234
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,367
- [GRUNTS]
- [MONITOR CLATTERS]

235
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,367
You are just like him.

236
00:11:44,733 --> 00:11:45,833
Ba-bye.

237
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:50,233
[SLAPS]

238
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:52,967
[COLE CHUCKLES WRYLY]

239
00:11:55,767 --> 00:12:02,767
[POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING]

240
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:09,967
[SNIFFLES]

241
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,400
[CRIES, SOBS]

242
00:12:15,433 --> 00:12:20,800
[POIGNANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

243
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:21,733
[SNIFFLES]

244
00:12:25,267 --> 00:12:29,367
[CRYING, SOBBING]

245
00:12:30,767 --> 00:12:33,833
[EXHALES, SOBBING]

246
00:12:36,933 --> 00:12:38,233
[SNIFFLES]

247
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:45,900
- [POIGNANT MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [SOBBING, SNIFFLING]

248
00:12:53,233 --> 00:12:55,033
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

249
00:12:58,133 --> 00:12:59,067
[DOOR CLICKS OPEN]

250
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,400
Hi.

251
00:13:01,933 --> 00:13:03,067
Oh, hi.

252
00:13:03,367 --> 00:13:04,400
Hmm.

253
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,467
I brought you these.

254
00:13:06,033 --> 00:13:07,867
[MARLA] Aw! Thank you.

255
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:10,000
How are you?

256
00:13:11,967 --> 00:13:13,233
I'm okay.

257
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,467
Thank you.

258
00:13:15,467 --> 00:13:16,967
Thank you for helping me.

259
00:13:17,233 --> 00:13:19,267
Had I read Nyx's message
earlier,

260
00:13:19,267 --> 00:13:20,800
I could have prevented this--

261
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:21,833
[MARLA] Shh.

262
00:13:21,867 --> 00:13:23,400
Stop blaming yourself.

263
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,800
It's okay.

264
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,033
I'm okay.

265
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,400
In fact, the doctors already
gave me clearance,

266
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:30,000
I can go back to school.

267
00:13:31,167 --> 00:13:33,800
Hey, can you sign my cast?

268
00:13:35,167 --> 00:13:37,400
I think there's
